IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tgr-patient`

-- Cases for tgr-patient.l4: Therapeutic Goods Regulations 1990 (Cth), from the seat of the patient.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the deposited text (and, for the 28 days in reg 12A(3), the Acts
-- Interpretation Act 1901 s 36 applied by the Legislation Act 2003 s 13(1)(a)), before the encoding was run.
-- Weekdays: 2 March 2026 and 30 March 2026 are Mondays; 14 February 2026 and 14 March 2026 are Saturdays.
-- The facts are invented. No real medicine, company or person is meant.
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Dates and periods`

#ASSERT `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 14 2 2026)
#ASSERT `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 2 3 2026))
-- 28 days after Monday 2 March 2026 is Monday 30 March 2026: not moved.
#ASSERT `day number of` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` (`the date` 2 3 2026)) EQUALS `day number of` (`the date` 30 3 2026)
-- 28 days after Saturday 14 February 2026 is Saturday 14 March 2026, moved to Monday 16 March (AIA s 36(2)).
#ASSERT `day number of` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` (`the date` 14 2 2026)) EQUALS `day number of` (`the date` 16 3 2026)

§ `Definitions`

-- reg 2 "immediate family": the person themself is not in it (Schedule 5 item 1 names the importer separately).
#ASSERT NOT (`is my immediate family` `my own`)
#ASSERT `is my immediate family` `my spouse or de facto partner`
#ASSERT `is my immediate family` `a child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of my spouse or de facto partner`
#ASSERT NOT (`is my immediate family` `someone else`)
#ASSERT `is for me or my immediate family` `my own`

-- reg 9B(4), (5): less than 8 weeks (56 days) of development, suspended time disregarded.
#ASSERT `is a human embryo` TRUE TRUE 55 0
#ASSERT NOT (`is a human embryo` TRUE TRUE 56 0)
#ASSERT `is a human embryo` TRUE TRUE 70 15
#ASSERT NOT (`is a human embryo` TRUE TRUE 71 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a human embryo` FALSE TRUE 10 0)

-- Schedule 10 Part 1: a Schedule 4 medicine; the same accepted into Part 2 or 3; an injectable; a complementary medicine.
#ASSERT `is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is in Part 1 of Schedule 10` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `The information that must come with my medicine (regs 9A, 9B, Schedules 12, 13)`

-- A prescription-only (Schedule 4) medicine on the Register: a Schedule 12 leaflet.
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) EQUALS `a document meeting Schedule 12 must come with it`
-- A vaccine (Schedule 10 Part 1 item 3): a Schedule 12 leaflet.
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) EQUALS `a document meeting Schedule 12 must come with it`
-- The same medicine, not on the Register (imported or compounded): reg 9A does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) EQUALS `regulation 9A requires no document for it`
-- A pharmacist-only (Schedule 3) medicine approved on 4 July 1995: Schedule 13. One approved on 3 July 1995: none.
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 4 7 1995) EQUALS `a document meeting Schedule 13 must come with it`
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`the date` 3 7 1995) EQUALS `regulation 9A requires no document for it`
-- A Schedule 3 injectable approved in 1990: in Part 1, but the (1AA) defence answers (1), and (1A) needs 4 July 1995.
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`the date` 1 1 1990) EQUALS `regulation 9A requires no document for it`
-- A complementary medicine (Schedule 10 Part 2), not scheduled: none.
#ASSERT `Must my medicine come with a consumer medicine information document` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) EQUALS `regulation 9A requires no document for it`

-- reg 9A penalty: 10 penalty units where the leaflet was needed and not supplied.
